customer: activist_guy
brief:
	He has seen what happens and leaves town. He just leaves his computer and leaves, without a problem: "I would recommend you stay away from tech as well." Digging deep in it finds his research. With a lot of time: he has downgraded his OS. His narrative ends here.

== drop-off
(neutral) Hello! Have you got a minute?
+ Nice button. What's it for?
	(happy) Saving the old park from the parking lot people. Sign our petition sometime!
+ Busy day?
	(neutral) Always. The newsletter doesn't write itself.
+ So, what's your problem?
	(problem) My computer counts up its memory, and then it just stops. It never gets to Windows.
	+ Did anything change lately?
		(neutral) My nephew put more memory in it last month. It was meant to be faster!
	- OK, leave it with me. [end]
		(neutral) I need it for the newsletter, so please be quick.

== pick-up
(happy) It starts again? Wonderful. I'll have a word with my nephew.
